dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.cad.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.cad
start body
framing record

# cad wave (following the workflow/brep pilots' proven template): REAL binary pack frame,
# replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s old
# `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly, PROVEN bare
# `segment` form per the workflow report's UPDATE §7 note) are genuinely, fully described. Past
# that, `layers`/`blocks`/`entities` are HOMOGENEOUS but variable-length repeated records (`blocks`
# itself holds a further variable-length `entities` sub-collection, and `blocks[].entities`/
# `entities` both embed a data-carrying tagged `entity` union) — the `protocol-array-of-records` gap
# (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field", for an
# untagged homogeneous record): modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest
# boundary every P1-P3/workflow/brep pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust
# `encode_cad_snapshot_binary`/`decode_cad_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully structured
# (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real `f64` LE coordinates, a real per-variant tag byte
# for `entity`) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol
# DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
